{"id":"charger","name":"Charger","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:charger"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Charger","text":"A bowl or deep dish. The silver vessels given by the heads of the tribes for the services of the tabernacle are so named (Num. 7:13, etc.). The “charger” in which the Baptist’s head was presented was a platter or flat wooden trencher (Matt. 14:8, 11; Mark 6:25, 28). The chargers of gold and silver of Ezra 1:9 were probably basins for receiving the blood of sacrifices."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7086","lemma":"קְעָרָה","xlit":"qᵉʻârâh","gloss":"a bowl","kjv":"charger, dish","count":14,"share":0.88},{"strong":"H4219","lemma":"מִזְרָק","xlit":"mizrâq","gloss":"a bowl","kjv":"bason, bowl","count":14,"share":0.88},{"strong":"H8255","lemma":"שֶׁקֶל","xlit":"sheqel","gloss":"probably a weight","kjv":"shekel","count":13,"share":0.81},{"strong":"H1101","lemma":"בָּלַל","xlit":"bâlal","gloss":"to overflow","kjv":"anoint, confound, fade, mingle","count":12,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H4948","lemma":"מִשְׁקָל","xlit":"mishqâl","gloss":"weight","kjv":"weight","count":12,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H5560","lemma":"סֹלֶת","xlit":"çôleth","gloss":"flour","kjv":"flour, meal","count":12,"share":0.75}],"verses":["Num.7.13","Num.7.19","Num.7.25","Num.7.31","Num.7.37","Num.7.43","Num.7.49","Num.7.55","Num.7.61","Num.7.67","Num.7.73","Num.7.79","Num.7.84","Num.7.85","Matt.14.8","Matt.14.11"],"related":[{"id":"bowl","type":"cooccur","shared":13,"jaccard":0.52,"why":"13 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"silver","type":"cooccur","shared":14,"jaccard":0.106,"why":"14 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"shekel","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.063,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"meat-offerings","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.049,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"altar-of-burnt-offering","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.031,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"bowl"